// Private canonical Linux x86_64 LP64 glibc import assembly. Main owns
// selected-native activation in Core/sys after stage1. This root never loads
// kernel32/ntdll or Darwin __error. Darwin LP64 uses darwin_os_imports.jet;
// Windows uses windows_file.jet and the separately selected ntdll unit.
//
// Raw pointer arguments borrow live initialized storage for the synchronous
// call only. Paths are caller-owned NUL-terminated OS bytes (Unix) or UTF16
// code units (Windows); never reinterpret a Jet String/list object as C data.
// Ownership of successful fd/HANDLE results transfers to the consumer, which
// closes exactly once on normal return and every early-error path. Borrowed
// calls never close; dup creates an independently closed owner of the same
// open file description. No #Close on I32: that would consume unrelated ints.
//
// Error capture must happen immediately after the failing OS call, before
// cleanup/formatting/scheduler entry. Raw errno/GetLastError are not a second
// IOError normalizer. The canonical IOError owner supplies classification/text.
// EINTR retry, partial IO loops, lock deadlines, secure descent, rewrite and
// process/namespace/seccomp policies remain the consumers' canonical owners.
//
// Native capability gates (reported to RuntimeLead-8 for #4494): C pointer
// return admission (errno/HANDLE); nested pointer/FixedList C-safe fields;
// nullable native function pointers + signal-safe callback lowering; native
// pointer-sized integer/size_t selection; retained contiguous initialized
// buffer provenance; canonical OS-code -> IOError boundary. #4467 is the
// independent #Import(c) scalar lowering defect, not a reason to alter libc.
module unix_fd
module linux_seccomp_imports
module process_control
